,"label":"Artists with disabilities","sourceId":"source-open-library-spring-will-come-william-n-zulu"}],"publicationYear":2005,"pageCount":372,"summary":"\"William Zulu has a natural flair for storytelling and his writing is informed and articulate. His wryly observant eye offers a fascinating window to the world of traditional Africa - with all its superstition, patriarchal rigidity and prejudices on the one hand, and its humour, shrewd observance and innovative survival strategies on the other. Reading his story, one is left with a vivid sense of the rural African battles for survival that pit ingenuity against lack of resources - and of the redemptive power of 'ubuntu', demonstrated in the kindness of strangers of all races, who extend helping hand and heart in the midst of spiritual and physical destitution. Spring Will Come is a story that lives up to its title.\"--BOOK JACKET.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/920797-L.jpg","experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Africa","confidence":0.82}],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Ubuntu has redemptive power, as kindness and solidarity help sustain people amid spiritual and physical destitution and severe resource shortages.","confidence":0.82},"academicOrientation":{"score":25,"confidence":0.78},"profileConfidence":0.84,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"769909575cddea2ef206e32695f36f3ee99e6bd2830ed652682b313a2683363b","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"His wryly observant eye offers a fascinating window to the world of traditional Africa - with all its superstition, patriarchal rigidity and prejudices on the one hand, and its humour, shrewd observance and innovative survival strategies on the other. Reading his story, one is left with a vivid sense of the rural African battles for survival that pit ingenuity against lack of resources - and of the redemptive power of 'ubuntu', demonstrated in the kind